Local fork edit for OpenBCI_32bit_SD library
============================================

File: <Arduino libraries dir>/OpenBCI_32bit_SD/utility/Sd2Card.h
Change: SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT 600 ms → 1500 ms
Date: 2026-05-13
Reason: pSLC / high-endurance SD cards (SanDisk Max Endurance, Industrial)
        do periodic background GC bursts that stall SPI for 200-500 ms.
        At 600 ms, every overrun fires the firmware's inline 5x writeStart
        retry → ~1 s of dropped samples per GC cycle (~6 events/min on
        Max Endurance 32 GB → see OBCI_B6.TXT 2026-05-13: e=565 r=1020).
        Raising to 1500 ms absorbs GC bursts up to ~1.5 s with NO sample
        loss. Worst-case downside: a truly dead-card recovery event takes
        ~1.5 s longer to declare failure, then the firmware's extended
        recovery loop in writeCache (also added 2026-05-13) takes over.

Re-apply manually after any reinstall of the SD library:

    sed -i 's/uint16_t const SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT = 600;/uint16_t const SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT = 1500;/' \
        ~/Arduino/libraries/OpenBCI_32bit_SD/utility/Sd2Card.h

Diff:

