+ * boundary - every GC overrun > 600 ms surfaced as a card.writeData() failure
+ * -> fired the inline 5x writeStart retry -> spent ~1 s of dropped samples per
+ * GC cycle. With 1500 ms ceiling, GC bursts up to ~1.5 s are absorbed
+ * silently with NO sample loss. Worst-case downside: a truly dead-card
+ * recovery event takes ~1.5 s longer to declare failure (the firmware's
+ * extended recovery loop in SD_Card_Stuff.ino's writeCache then takes over).
+ *
+ * NOTE: this is a local fork edit - the file lives outside the OpenBCI
+ * firmware repo (~/Arduino/libraries/OpenBCI_32bit_SD/). Re-apply if
+ * the SD library is reinstalled.
+ */
+uint16_t const SD_WRITE_TIMEOUT = 1500;
